  "term": "basic-level category",
  "definition": "A basic-level category is a more specific class within a broader category, such as “bird” or “dog” within “animal.” In visual categorization, identifying this level can take longer and be less accurate than deciding the broader superordinate category, especially when other members of the same broad class are present.",
